\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 /**\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * INVENTORY / CALIBRATE / COUNT AUTOMATION\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * ------------------------------------------\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * Sheets involved:\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   - "Inventory"        Col B (2) = item name\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         Col C (3) = locations, comma-separated (e.g. "A10,2B1,11A")\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         Col D (4) = quantity\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   - "Calibrate Cycle"  B3 = number of days\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         A5 = dropdown: MENU / Calibrate / Clear / Refresh\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   - "Records"          B2 = cycle name (user-entered)\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         A3 = dropdown: CYCLE MENU / NEW CYCLE\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         Row 5 = Day 1, Day 2, ... (one per column, starting col A)\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         Row 6 = "Started" / completion date, under the matching day column\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         A7 = dropdown: COUNT MENU / START / COMPLETE\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         B8 = dropdown: SELECT / Day 1 / Day 2 / ...\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         Row 11+ = permanent discrepancy log table (never cleared)\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   - "Count"             Results written starting row 2.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         Col B = item name, Col H = quantity (system-filled)\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         Col C = multiply x, Col D = multiply y (per detail row)\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         Col E = addition, Col F = subtract (per detail row)\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         Col G = Total, Col I = Difference (computed), Col J = Note (user-filled)\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *                         A1 = dropdown: MENU / COUNT\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * ============================= CALIBRATE CYCLE =============================\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   - "Clear": wipes row 11+ in Calibrate Cycle, resets A5 to "MENU".\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   - "Calibrate": pulls Inventory items with quantity > 0, splits them across\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     B3 "Calibrate Day" groups so each day's total quantity is as balanced\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     as possible (LPT algorithm), writes result from row 11, resets A5.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   - "Refresh": re-pulls current quantities for items already in the table\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     (does not change which items/days exist), updates col C and day\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     Totals in col E, resets A5. Items no longer in Inventory -> qty 0.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * ================================= RECORDS ==================================\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   CYCLE MENU (A3):\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   - "NEW CYCLE": counts how many "Calibrate Day N" blocks exist in\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     Calibrate Cycle (col A, from row 11 down), clears + rewrites row 5\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     with "Day 1", "Day 2", ... (starting col A), clears row 6 as well,\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     rebuilds the B8 dropdown as SELECT + each day, sets B8 to "SELECT",\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     resets A3 to "CYCLE MENU".\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   COUNT MENU (A7):\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   - "START": reads B8. If "SELECT", does nothing (just resets A7).\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     Otherwise writes "Started" in row 6 under the matching day column,\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     finds the matching "Calibrate Day N" block in Calibrate Cycle, grabs\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     its item names, looks up fresh quantity + locations for each item\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     from Inventory (locations sorted ascending by leading number, items\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     with no leading number sorted last), and sends the result as a JSON\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     array of [item, "loc1,loc2,...", quantity] entries via a POST request\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     to the external counting server (SERVER_BASE_URL +\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     SERVER_START_ENDPOINT), authenticated with the "YOUR_API_KEY" Script\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     Property. The Count sheet is no longer written to by START. Resets\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     A7 to "COUNT MENU" when done.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   - "COMPLETE": scans the Count sheet for item rows where Total (col G)\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     is a number and doesn't equal Quantity (col H), OR Note (col J) is\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     non-empty. For each such row, appends one row to the Records log\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     table (row 11+, never cleared) with: cycle name (B2), cycle day (B8),\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     today's date (America/New_York), item name, total, quantity,\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     difference, note. Then, regardless of whether any log rows were\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     added, writes today's date into row 6 under the matching day column\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     (replacing "Started") to mark that day's count as complete. Resets\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     A7 to "COUNT MENU" when done.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * ================================== COUNT ===================================\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   A1 dropdown:\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *   - "COUNT": for every non-item (detail/location) row: multiply term =\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     x * y (col C * col D); if only one of x/y is filled, the other is\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     treated as 1; if both are blank, the multiply term is 0. Addition\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     (col E) and subtract (col F) are added/subtracted only if filled in\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     (blank = skipped, contributes 0). Row total = multiply + addition -\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     subtract, written to col G. If a detail row has all four inputs\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     blank, its col G is left blank (not zeroed) since there's nothing to\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     carry. Each item row's Total (col G) is then set to the sum of all\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     its detail rows' totals, and its Difference (col I) is set to\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     Total - Quantity (col H), only when Quantity is a number. Also\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     applies background colors: cols C:D light yellow, col E light green,\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     col F light red, col G light blue, and each full item row light gray\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     (overriding the column colors on that row). Resets A1 to "MENU" when\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *     done.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  */\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 var\cf4 \strokec4  \cf6 \strokec6 CALIBRATE_SHEET_NAME\cf4 \strokec4  = \cf7 \strokec7 "Calibrate Cycle"\cf4 \strokec4 ;\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 var\cf4 \strokec4  \cf6 \strokec6 INVENTORY_SHEET_NAME\cf4 \strokec4  = \cf7 \strokec7 "Inventory"\cf4 \strokec4 ;\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 var\cf4 \strokec4  \cf6 \strokec6 RECORDS_SHEET_NAME\cf4 \strokec4    = \cf7 \strokec7 "Records"\cf4 \strokec4 ;\cb1 \
